      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T07:48:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s too new. Also I don\u0027t know if this is a candidate for stable tree as it is not a fix as such but a workaround-and-warning for incorrect behaviour. It\u0027s a nice to have, as it would have made root causing b/258019933 easier.",
      "parentUuid": "56bb1339_b90e14f0",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd586bca_5f15febb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T08:27:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it is relevant for our trees as a bugfix, then it should also be in the upstream stable releases.  Please submit it there first and then we can easily take it into the branches here.",
      "parentUuid": "06f8eb47_b600a724",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15f09e6c_3e01d6c5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1935515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T08:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a tough call because it\u0027s not a fix. The bug it *works around* in the UFS driver polling implementation is not even in upstream 5.15: We see it because we backported the 5.19 UFS driver.",
      "parentUuid": "fd586bca_5f15febb",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "935ee561_c63d3997",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T08:39:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then why isn\u0027t it relevant for the 6.0.y stable kernel branch?",
      "parentUuid": "15f09e6c_3e01d6c5",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fd71203_467692f9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1935515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T08:48:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The actual fix is being worked on upstream right now. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s quite right yet but it\u0027s WIP, see https://lore.kernel.org/linux-scsi/20221114233042.3199381-1-bvanassche@acm.org/T/#u\n\nThis workaround-and-warn patch is relevant to 6.0.x, agreed. But wouldn\u0027t the final tested actual fix(es) be the ones taken to stable?\n\nHere would be my reasoning to take this patch to 5.15+ stable: The code it adds warning to makes a fragile assumption about polling completion occurring in process context. Drivers can easily break this (seen in UFS driver). This patch avoids a crash and gives a useful backtrace, making debugging so much easier.\n\nIf that ^ seems reasonable, I\u0027ll give it a shot.",
      "parentUuid": "935ee561_c63d3997",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69a7a91a_64c59d00",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T12:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, documenting why this is needed because of the UFS changes is required in order for us to properly review this.  Please add some text to the changelog for this.",
      "parentUuid": "935ee561_c63d3997",
      "revId": "3d382dd8007bebbb067e53671f0b6b1758950b77",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
